    "result_text": "All 61 tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new `Cp49Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a `selfLink` field to the owner resource, returning `/api/owners/<id>`.\n\nTwo edits, following the codebase's existing conventions for derived owner fields:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `selfLink` string property to the `Owner` schema (right after `id`). The DTOs are generated from this spec at build time, so this creates the `getSelfLink()`/`setSelfLink()` accessors on the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that populates `selfLink` as `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()` (null-guarded on both `owner` and its `id`, matching the existing expressions in that mapper).\n\nThis is exactly how the other derived read-only fields (`customerCode`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, etc.) are wired, so the value is computed uniformly for the create response and the `GET /api/owners/{id}` read-back the test uses.",
